From 34951dd413790f0f53e8df5f153674c092d14e09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:25:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): macOS Cmd+Q asks about unsaved changes

winit 0.30's default app menu Quit (Cmd+Q) sends terminate: to
NSApplication, and winit's app delegate has no
applicationShouldTerminate:, so the process ended at once and the
Save / Don't Save / Cancel prompt (#107) was skipped. The same path
serves the Dock's Quit, quit Apple Events and logout.

egui_app/os_quit.rs adds applicationShouldTerminate: to winit's
delegate class at startup (class_addMethod via objc2 0.5, already in
the lock; macOS only). It cancels the terminate and raises a flag that
the shell's about_to_wait turns into the same guarded Quit command the
window X queues, bringing the window forward for the prompt. If winit
ever ships its own handler, the add is refused, logged, and winit's
behaviour stands.

Pinned by os_quit_request_over_unsaved_changes_prompts_once.

Fixes #144

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
